        {
          "id": "the_PM10_chain_is_a_ratio_lookup_with_a_model_year_range",
          "description": "PM10BrakeTireCalculator, entirely. `pm10emissionratio` gives 8.0 for model years 1940-2010 and 2.60985 for 2011-2060 on the three combustion fuels, 1.42475 on electricity -- so a document that dropped the range predicate would be a factor of three out on half the rows and one that dropped the fuel key would be 83 % out on the electricity ones. The ratio is 0 on the two unchained rate paths, because `pm10emissionratio` carries polProcessID 10609 and nothing else, and that zero is what makes `rtDay_quantChained` vanish there without a branch. `rtDay_quantDirect` is asserted at exactly 0 on a chained row for the mirror reason: `emissionrate` has no 10609 row, so J22's inner join leaves its rate at the additive identity and the chained block's whole quantity comes through the chain.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_chainRatio",
              "time": 0.0,
